 const HELPF=()=>{const c=CT(),sc=SCHEME(),K1=k1;return[
  ['CONTROLS',sc==='touch'?`Steer: ${c.steer}. Speed: ${c.speed}. Fire: ${c.fire}.\nThe buttons along the flight deck do everything else: MSL (missile), ECM, JUMP, DOCK, HYPER, TIME, the view button (FRONT, REAR…), CAM, BOMB, POD, HOLD, MISN, MAP, TIPS and MENU. Tap a button once to see what it does (hover help).\nPause with the arcade’s Pause button or the MENU key on the deck.`:
   `Steer: ${c.steer}.\nSpeed: ${c.speed} (the mouse wheel works too). ${c.boost}. ${c.extra}${sc==='modern'?' Q and E roll.':''}\nFire the laser: ${c.fire}. Missile: ${K1('missile')} (once you have a MISSILE LOCK).\n${sc==='modern'&&STYLE()==='modern'&&C.opt.cock3d?'Look around the 3D cockpit: hold the RIGHT mouse button and drag. In full screen on a wide display, the console has switches and knobs on both sides — click them (hover for help). In a smaller window, move the mouse to the bottom edge for the switch bar (📌 keeps it open).\n':''}Views: 1–4 = front, rear, left, right · ${K1('cam')} = outside camera.\nPause: P or Esc. Hover help on/off: ${K1('tips')}. Cockpit screens: ${K1('mfd')}.\nThe CONTROLS tab lists every key — click one to change it. MODERN uses the mouse; CLASSIC is keyboard only.`],
  ['DOCKING',`Every station spins. Its docking slot is the glowing rectangle facing the planet.\n1. Fly towards the station — the compass points at it and the radar shows it as a white square.\n2. Slow right down (below 60 on the speed bar SP).\n3. Press ${K1('spin')} to match the station’s spin (or ${K1('rlock')} to lock your own roll), then point straight at the slot.\n4. Fly in gently — follow the glowing corridor frames (green = lined up, slow and spin-matched). Wrong angle, wrong spin or too fast = a crash!\nEasy way: buy a DOCKING COMPUTER (tech level 9+) and press ${K1('dock')} (DOCK) near the station.`],
  ['TRADING',`Buy goods where they are cheap and sell where they are dear.\n• Farming worlds sell food, spices and plants cheaply and pay well for machines and computers. Factory worlds are the opposite.\n• Market keys: ↑ ↓ choose a product, → or + buys one, ← or − sells one, Enter buys as much as you can.\n• The PAID and PROFIT columns show what you paid and what you would make. 📈 TREND shows a price graph.\n• Prices move when you trade: buying lots pushes a price up, selling lots pushes it down.\n• Illegal goods (⚠) pay well, but customs and police scans may catch you.`],
  ['COMBAT',`Put the enemy in your sights and fire (${c.fire}). Lasers lock on to a target for a few seconds; getting hit breaks the lock. Let them cool if they overheat.\n• Missiles: keep a ship in your sights until MISSILE LOCK shows, then press ${K1('missile')}.\n• Select a target with ${K1('scan')} or by tapping the radar. Press ${K1('subsys')} to aim at its engines or weapons.\n• E.C.M. (${K1('ecm')}) destroys missiles fired at you. Shock pulse (${K1('bomb')}) hits every ship nearby, once.\n• A hired wingman protects you — press ${K1('wingman')} to send them after your target.\n• Shipyard extras: Starburst laser (${K1('starburst')} — spins and blasts every hostile ship close by) and the fire-control computer (${K1('firectl')} — locks on and fires for you for 20 seconds).\n• Pirates earn bounties. Attacking traders or police makes you an Offender or Fugitive.`],
  ['TRAVEL',`• Jump drive (${K1('jump')}): races across a system. It won’t work near ships, stations, planets or hazards.\n• Time (${K1('time')}): speeds up long trips; it stops if danger appears.\n• Hyperspace: press ${K1('chart')} for the chart, pick a system in range (the 3D MAP plans longer routes), then press ${K1('hyper')}. It uses fuel (light years).\n• Radar range: ${K1('radarRange')} switches between 5, 10 and 25 km.\n• Watch out for asteroid fields, pirate minefields and black holes!\n• Escape capsule (${K1('pod')}, press twice) saves your credits if all else fails.`],
  ['MISSIONS',`Station bulletin boards (MISSIONS tab) offer:\n• Courier, supply runs and Wanted pirates — and Freedom / Expansion jobs that change how a planet is ruled.\n• 🧳 Passengers (a tip if you are quick), ⛏️ mining contracts, and 🏁 station races through 8 gates against the clock.\n• Story missions (⭐ The Vorn Signal, 🛰️ The Lost Freighter), and ⚖️ Amnesty jobs to clear your name.\n• 🎓 Academy (daily) and 🏆 Navigator’s Cup (weekly, on your trickiest topics). 🤝 Hire a wingman for 3 jumps.\nIn flight, press ${K1('missions')} (MISN) for your MISSION LOG — where you are, what is left and your next step — and ${K1('cargo')} (HOLD) for your cargo.`],
  ['EXTRAS',`• Survey planets, moons and stars: fly slowly close to them until the survey bar fills, then sell the data when you dock.\n• Rescue survivors from escape pods by flying into them slowly.\n• Your Career record (${K1('career')}) shows your fortune, fame, reputation, medals and maths rank.\n• Maths puzzles earn bonuses and Navigator ranks; get one wrong and you will see how to work it out.\n• 🌌 A galactic hyperdrive (tech 10) jumps you to the next of 8 galaxies — use it from the CHART at a station.\n• 🪑 At a station, LAUNCH tab → COCKPIT: FLIGHT CONTROLS (your normal cockpit, looking into the shuttle bay) or COCKPIT: PRE-FLIGHT VIEW (a checklist). Look around, then launch from there.\n• 🧸 Make the cockpit your own: the SHIPYARD’s PERSONAL tab sells dice, a bobble-head, a plant, fairy lights and more (Modern style). Display → LIVED-IN COCKPIT turns the clutter on or off.\n• 🎓 TOURS (pause menu): watch Nova fly any part of the game, with the keys and mouse shown. They use a practice game.\n• 💾 SAVE AS… / 📂 OPEN… (pause menu): keep named saves and go back to them — opening one keeps your game as “Where I was”.`]];};
